<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Is Spacemaker AI included with Autodesk AEC Collection?</div><div class="faq-answer">Spacemaker may be available as an add-on to AEC Collection subscriptions, but specific availability varies by region and licensing agreement. Contact Autodesk for details on bundling options.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">What's the minimum project size for Spacemaker to be worthwhile?</div><div class="faq-answer">Spacemaker is most cost-effective for projects with multiple buildings or significant site complexity. Generally, developments with 50+ residential units or mixed-use projects above 50,000 sq ft benefit most from the platform.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can Spacemaker integrate with non-Autodesk software?</div><div class="faq-answer">While optimized for Autodesk products, Spacemaker can export to standard formats like IFC and DWG. However, the deepest integration and most seamless workflows are with Revit and other Autodesk tools.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">How accurate are the environmental simulations?</div><div class="faq-answer">Spacemaker's simulations use validated algorithms and real-world climate data, providing results suitable for early design decisions and feasibility studies. For final certification, detailed analysis with specialized tools is still recommended.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Is training included with the license?</div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, enterprise licenses typically include onboarding training and ongoing support. Autodesk also offers advanced training programs for teams who want to maximize their use of the platform.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can multiple team members work on the same project?</div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, Spacemaker includes robust collaboration features allowing multiple users to work on projects simultaneously. Projects can be shared within teams and version control is built-in.</div></div>
